# {{lb|en|informal}} A very [[rapid]]ly moving object, especially one that is [[throw]]n.
#: {{ux|en|The pitcher threw a real '''zinger''' and struck him out.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|title= |author=Joseph Sutton  |page= |ISBN=0965597466 |passage=On the first pitch from Kline, Lofton hits a '''zinger''' of a single into right field that J.D. Drew picks up on one bounce, and if he makes a good throw he has a chance to throw David Bell out at home plate. }}
# {{lb|en|informal}} A [[surprising]] or unusually [[pointed]], humorous and impressive insult or insulting quip.
#: {{syn|en|one-liner}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|title=Seasons in Time  |author= Larry Groves |page=112 |ISBN=1465328815 |passage=I wasn't looking to make friends; there had been too much animosity between us in the past, and maybe the guy had a '''zinger''' waiting on me. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|title=The Third Space |author=Adam Fraser |page=124 |ISBN=9781742753867 |passage=You might think it's almost worthwhile calling them and restarting the argument just to get that final '''zinger''' in. Why do you think of something good to say when it's too late?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=David Segal|title=An Outsider Takes an Inside Look at the Oxford ‘Chums’ Who Run the U.K.|work=The New York Times|date=2022-05-14|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/14/books/simon-kuper-book-oxford.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=Boris Johnson is the most compelling personality in “Chums.” The shambolic style, the self-deprecating humor, the gift for '''zingers'''—it was all there in university, as was the elitist’s ambivalent approach to achievement.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} An event that when experienced leaves the witness [[daze]]d, either physically or metaphorically.
#: {{ux|en|I was still reeling from the '''zinger''' of seeing my ex on a date with my best friend.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} An outstanding, energetic and surprising thing or person.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006 |title=My Beloved Bohemian  |author=Olivia Hillis Wimbrow  |page=130 |ISBN=0741432897 |passage= They'd have to come up with a '''zinger''' for their Christmas windows to compete with that competitor's laughing Santa Claus and Stefan had that '''zinger''' in his proposal submitted to the President of the company.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006 |title=Done Gone Wrong |author=Cathy Pickens  |page= |ISBN=142990786X |passage=Think about all the scientists—and all the microscopes and lab equipment and testing—that may come up with zero instead of a '''zinger'''. }}
# Something to eat or drink that is [[tart]] and [[stimulating]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|title=Rescue Princesses #5: The Snow Jewel
|author=Paula Harrison  |page= |ISBN=0545509319 |passage=Here, have a strawberry '''zinger''' and don't tell Mom and Dad that we had candy in the bedroom. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016 |title=The Rain Sparrow |author=Linda Goodnight  |page= |ISBN=1489208119 |passage=“Want some—” he saluted her with one of Julia's delicate white cups and a wry arch of eyebrow, sipped and made a face “—lemon '''zinger''' tea?” At times like this she wished she was as outgoing as Nikki or gorgeous like Bailey or even a little wild and easy with men like Valery. But she was none of those things. She was plain Carrie, the librarian, wishing she could say something snappy and clever. “If you don't like lemon '''zinger''', pick a different kind." }}